WHERE TO GET YOUR google-services.json
======================================
1. Go to: console.firebase.google.com
2. Create a new project (any name)
3. Click "Add App" → Android
4. Package name: com.karan.distancewidget
5. Download google-services.json
6. Put it in THIS folder (app/)
7. In Firebase console → Realtime Database → Create Database → Test Mode
8. Set rules to:
   {
     "rules": {
       ".read": true,
       ".write": true
     }
   }
9. Delete this .PLACEHOLDER file

DO NOT commit google-services.json to git.
